#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide2.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive2.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:45
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:449
msgid "First let’s review the structure of this session."
msgstr "Commençons par revoir la structure de cette session."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:47
msgid "In the section on DEFINITIONS we will first try to clarify the use of the word “Data”."
msgstr "Dans la section sur les DEFINITIONS nous allons d'abord essayer de clarifier l'utilisation du mot \"Données\"."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:49
msgid "We will then look at the terminology surrounding Fields, Labels and Lists."
msgstr "Nous examinerons ensuite la terminologie entourant Champs, Étiquettes et Listes."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:51
msgid "And lastly, we will straighten out some concepts around characters and their mappings that will help prevent unwanted data messes."
msgstr "Enfin, nous allons clarifier certains concepts relatifs aux caractères et à leurs conversions, ce qui permettra d'éviter les erreurs de données indésirables."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide3.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive3.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 3 - Definitions*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 3 - Définitions*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:57
msgid "First definitions."
msgstr "Premières définitions."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:59
msgid "In this section we will look at some of the many different terms and phrases that exist within the world of data and information management."
msgstr "Dans cette section, nous allons examiner quelques-uns des nombreux termes et expressions qui existent dans le monde de la gestion des données et de l'information."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:61
msgid "We will be using these throughout the course and it is important that you be familiar with, when and how to use them."
msgstr "Nous les utiliserons tout au long du cours et il est important que vous soyez familier avec, et sachiez quand et comment les utiliser."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:63
msgid "Image by Sharon Grant: https://www.flickr.com/photos/rondls_pics/3629532537/in/album-72157619834323354/"
msgstr "Image de Sharon Grant : https://www.flickr.com/photos/rondls_pics/3629532537/in/album-72157619834323354/"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide4.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive4.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 4 - Definitions - a rose by any other name*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 4 - Définitions - Une rose, quel que soit son nom*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:69
msgid "Let’s focus for a moment on some common words and phrases that contain the word data."
msgstr "Nous allons nous concentrer un instant sur quelques expressions communes qui contiennent le mot donnée."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide5.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive5.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 5 - What's the difference - Database*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 5 - Quelle est la différence ? - Base de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:75
msgid "All of the phrases here include the word data, but are they all the same, and if not, then what is the difference?"
msgstr "Toutes les phrases ici incluent le mot donnée, mais sont-elles toutes les mêmes, et si ce n'est pas le cas, alors quelle est la différence?"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide6.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive6.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 6 - Database*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 6 - Base de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:81
msgid "So, what is a “Database”?"
msgstr "Alors, qu’est-ce qu’une “base de données”?"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:83
msgid "There are many definitions, but what they all have in common is the theme that a database is a structured and organized collection of data and/or information held on a computer."
msgstr "Il y a de nombreuses définitions, mais ce qu'ils ont tous en commun est le fait qu'une base de données est une collection structurée et organisée de données et/ou d'informations détenues sur un ordinateur."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:84
msgid "Everything else in the list is just a way to help you achieve this data nirvana!"
msgstr "Tout le reste de la liste est juste un moyen de vous aider à réaliser ce nirvana de données!"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:85
msgid "Let’s dig a little deeper then into those other terms."
msgstr "Approfondissons donc un peu ces autres termes."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide7.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive7.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 7 - Database language*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 7 - Langage de base de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:91
msgid "Let us take a look at the phrase “database language”."
msgstr "Examinons l'expression \"langage de base de données\"."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:93
msgid "According to the Oxford English dictionary “language” is the method of human communication...consisting of the use of words (or symbols) in a structured and conventional way."
msgstr "Selon l’Oxford English Dictionary, le langage est une forme de communication humaine qui utilise des mots ou des symboles de manière structurée et conventionnelle."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:95
msgid "For our purposes, database languages and their close allies the array languages are the way by which a human communicates with a computer to manipulate and move around data."
msgstr "Pour nos besoins, les langages de la base de données et leurs alliés proches, les langage des tableaux sont la façon par laquelle un humain communique avec un ordinateur pour manipuler et déplacer les données."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:97
msgid "Examples that you may have come across are:"
msgstr "Les exemples que vous pouvez rencontrer sont:"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:99
msgid "Java, SPARQL, SQL and Python"
msgstr "Java, SPARQL, SQL et Python"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:100
msgid "They are simply methods used to define and create tables, views and queries and also allow users to access, update, store and move data around."
msgstr "Ce sont simplement des méthodes utilisées pour définir et créer des tables, des vues et des requêtes, et permettre aussi aux utilisateurs d’accéder, de mettre à jour, de stocker et de déplacer des données."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide8.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive8.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 8 - Database program/software*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 8 – Programme ou logiciel de base de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:106
msgid "Now let’s look at the phrase “database program or software”."
msgstr "Voyons maintenant l'expression « programme ou logiciel de base de données »."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:108
msgid "Again going to the Oxford English dictionary a “program/programme” is a set of related measures or activities with a particular long-term aim."
msgstr "Une fois de plus, dans le dictionnaire anglais d'Oxford, un \"programme\" est un ensemble de mesures ou d'activités connexes avec un objectif particulier à long terme."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:110
msgid "In this context, a “database program or software” combines and presents functions and features for manipulating data, together is a unified interface."
msgstr "Dans ce contexte, un \"programme de base de données ou logiciel\" combine et présente des fonctions et des fonctionnalités pour manipuler les données, ensemble est une interface unifiée."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:112
msgid "Examples that you may come across are:"
msgstr "Les exemples que vous pouvez rencontrer sont:"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:114
msgid "Microsoft Access, FilemakerPro and Oracle"
msgstr "Microsoft Access, FilemakerPro et Oracle"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:116
msgid "So, database programs or software are grouped utilities which allow a user, via a database language, to store, manage, query and report data held in the system."
msgstr "Ainsi, les programmes ou logiciels de base de données sont des services regroupés qui permettent à un utilisateur, via un langage de base de données, de stocker, gérer, interroger et rapporter les données conservées dans le système."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide9.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive9.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 9 - Data cleaning tool*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 9 - Outil de nettoyage des données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:122
msgid "The last term is “data cleaning tool”."
msgstr "Le dernier terme est \"outil de nettoyage des données\"."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:124
msgid "Data cleaning tools are systems whose utilities focus is on the manipulation of data with the aim of increasing fitness for use."
msgstr "Les outils de nettoyage des données sont des systèmes conçus pour manipuler et améliorer les données afin de les rendre plus adaptées à l’usage prévu."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:126
msgid "Examples that you may be familiar or will learn about during the course are:"
msgstr "Des exemples que vous connaissez peut-être ou que vous apprendrez au cours de la formation sont:"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:128
msgid "OpenRefine, MatLab and spreadsheets"
msgstr "OpenRefine, MatLab et les feuilles de calcul"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:130
msgid "A data cleaning tool should assist the user in the discovery and repair of messy data in order to increase quality."
msgstr "Un outil de nettoyage des données devrait aider l'utilisateur à découvrir et à corriger des données confuses afin d'en améliorer la qualité."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide10.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive10.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 10 - Definitions - a rose by any other name*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 10 - Définitions - Une rose, quel que soit son nom*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:136
msgid "Continuing on with some more terms that you should be familiar with we will look at the differences between the terms Field, Label and List."
msgstr "En poursuivant avec d'autres termes avec lesquels vous devriez être familier, nous examinerons les différences entre les termes Champ, Étiquette et Liste."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide11.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive11.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:140
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 11 - Field vs label*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 11 - Champ vs étiquette*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:142
msgid "You will often hear reference made to field or column names and field labels or headings. Often they will be used interchangeably, however they are different things."
msgstr "On parle souvent de noms de champs ou de colonnes et de libellés ou d’en-têtes de champs, parfois comme s’il s’agissait de la même chose. Pourtant, ces termes ont des significations différentes."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:144
msgid "Field or column names refer to the actual column in the database table. They are a often short, not always in plain language, sometimes computer generated; but in a properly formed database they are ALWAYS unique. Field names are almost always used by database languages, because the avoid ambiguity."
msgstr "Les noms de champs ou de colonnes correspondent aux véritables identifiants des colonnes dans une table de base de données. Ils sont généralement courts, parfois peu explicites ou générés automatiquement. Dans une base de données bien structurée, chaque nom de champ est unique.\n"
"Les langages de base de données utilisent principalement ces noms uniques afin d’identifier les champs sans risque de confusion."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:146
msgid "Labels and headers on the other hand, refer to the human readable versions of the field names. Most often you will see these in the graphical user interface of your software and on exports and reports. In some software you can in fact have different labels to the same field on a user by user or group basis!"
msgstr "Les libellés et les en-têtes, en revanche, sont des versions plus faciles à comprendre des noms de champs. Ils apparaissent généralement dans l’interface graphique du logiciel, ainsi que dans les fichiers exportés et les rapports.\n"
"Dans certains logiciels, un même champ peut même avoir des libellés différents selon l’utilisateur ou le groupe d’utilisateurs."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide12.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive12.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 12 - Lists*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 12 - Listes*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:152
msgid "As you work with your data you will come across the phrases “drop-down list” and “controlled vocabulary” and on the surface they can appear to be the same. Indeed they are both powerful tools to help you keep your data clean, but they are different."
msgstr "Lorsque vous travaillez avec vos données, vous rencontrerez les termes « liste déroulante » et « vocabulaire contrôlé ». À première vue, ils peuvent sembler désigner la même chose. Tous deux sont en effet des outils très utiles pour maintenir la qualité et la cohérence de vos données, mais ils sont différents."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:154
msgid "A drop-down list, also sometimes called a lookup table is a data entry element that is created in your database software. It allows to you select a value from a predefined set of options. They can also be generated from the data itself on the fly."
msgstr "Une liste déroulante, parfois également appelée table de référence, est un élément de saisie configuré dans votre logiciel de base de données. Elle permet de sélectionner une valeur parmi un ensemble prédéfini d’options. Ces options peuvent aussi être générées automatiquement à partir des données existantes."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:156
msgid "A controlled vocabulary on the other hand, is a very strictly defined, domain specific set of values that should be applied to a particular field. They are an integral part of a well defined standard. Such values can be used in a drop-down list as mentioned previously."
msgstr "Un vocabulaire contrôlé, en revanche, est un ensemble de valeurs précisément définies pour un domaine particulier et destinées à être utilisées dans un champ spécifique. Il fait partie intégrante d’un standard clairement établi. Les valeurs d’un vocabulaire contrôlé peuvent notamment être proposées dans une liste déroulante, comme indiqué précédemment."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide13.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive13.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 13 - Definitions - a rose by any other name*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 13 - Définitions - Une rose, quel que soit son nom*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:162
msgid "In this section we will look at what the term character means in relation to data and computers."
msgstr "Dans cette section, nous examinerons ce que le terme caractère signifie par rapport aux données et aux ordinateurs."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide14.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive14.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 14 - Characters*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 14 – Caractères*"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:168
msgid "As a reminder computers “see” in binary. Everything that you type in, is held in memory as a series of ones and zeros."
msgstr "Pour rappel, les ordinateurs \"voient\" en binaire. Tout ce que vous tapez est conservé en mémoire sous la forme d'une série de uns et de zéros."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "The computer does not “see” the repertoire of letters and symbols on your keyboard.\n"
"\\vIt needs a map to translate the character set that you would write or type, into its binary language and then back again to show it to you on the screen or a printer.\n"
msgstr "L’ordinateur ne reconnaît pas directement les lettres et les symboles saisis à l’aide du clavier.\n"
"Il a besoin d’un système de correspondance pour convertir ces caractères en code binaire, puis les reconvertir afin de les afficher à l’écran ou de les reproduire sur une imprimante."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:173
msgid "This map is made up of two parts:"
msgstr "Cette carte est composée de deux parties :"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:175
msgid "The “coded character set”"
msgstr "Le « jeu de caractères codés »"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:177
msgid "and"
msgstr "et"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:179
msgid "The “character encoding”"
msgstr "L'\"encodage des caractères\""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:181
msgid "Each symbol or glyph is assigned a numeric value and that number is then converted to binary."
msgstr "Chaque symbole ou glyphe est assigné à une valeur numérique et ce nombre est ensuite converti en binaire."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide15.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive15.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:185
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 15 - Characters example*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 15 – Exemple de caractères codés*"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:187
msgid "In this example we see how character encoding is used to map the capital letter A in the western alphabet."
msgstr "Dans cet exemple, nous voyons comment l'encodage des caractères est utilisé pour mettre en correspondance la lettre majuscule A dans l'alphabet occidental."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:189
msgid "The ASCII value for the capital letter A is the decimal number 65"
msgstr "Dans le code ASCII, la lettre majuscule « A » correspond au nombre décimal 65"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:191
msgid "which in HEXIDECIMAL is 041"
msgstr "qui en HEXADECIMAL est 041"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:193
msgid "and in BINARY 01000001"
msgstr "et en BINAIRE 01000001"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:195
msgid "Try mapping your own name to Binary using the link at the bottom of the screen."
msgstr "Essayez de mapper votre propre nom au binaire en utilisant le lien en bas de l'écran."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide16.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive16.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:199
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 16 - Characters comparison*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 16 – Comparaison des caractères*"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:201
msgid "In effect what is happening is that when you type into a keyboard and save a file the software that you are using will select an encoding to save with it."
msgstr "En effet, ce qui se passe est que lorsque vous tapez dans un clavier et que vous enregistrez un fichier, le logiciel que vous utilisez sélectionnera un encodage à sauvegarder avec."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:203
msgid "When you open that file again the software needs to know which encoding (map) to use to redisplay the information back to you correctly."
msgstr "Lorsque vous ouvrez à nouveau ce fichier, le logiciel doit savoir quel encodage (carte) utiliser pour réafficher les informations correctement."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide17.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive17.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 17 - Characters*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:209
msgid "So why is this important to you as a data custodian?"
msgstr "Alors pourquoi est-ce important pour vous en tant que dépositaire de données ?"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:211
msgid "Let’s say that you translate the start of Hamlet’s soliloquy"
msgstr "Disons que vous traduisez le début du soliloque d'Hamlet"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:213
msgid " ”To be or not to be, that is the question”"
msgstr " \"Être ou ne pas être, c'est la question\""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:215
msgid "into French and then save the file with a text editor that uses the encoding Latin-1"
msgstr "en français puis enregistrez le fichier avec un éditeur de texte qui utilise l'encodage Latin-1"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:217
msgid "Then you send it to a colleague to check the translation. Voila!"
msgstr "Puis vous l'envoyez à un collègue pour vérifier la traduction. Voila!"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide18.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive18.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:221
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 18 - Characters*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 18 – Caractères*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:223
msgid "When they open the file in MicroSoft Word this is what they see."
msgstr "Quand ils ouvrent le fichier dans MicroSoft Word c'est ce qu'ils voient."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:225
msgid "Mon dieu!"
msgstr "Mon dieu!"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:227
msgid "There are some unexpected characters."
msgstr "Il y a des caractères inattendus."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:229
msgid "You forgot to tell your colleague that you where using Latin-1 as the encoding."
msgstr "Vous avez oublié de dire à votre collègue que vous utilisiez le Latin-1 comme encodage."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:231
msgid "MicroSoft Word on their end was set to use the encoding set Unicode UTF-8. The maps did not match."
msgstr "MicroSoft Word à leur extrémité a été configuré pour utiliser l'ensemble d'encodage Unicode UTF-8. Les cartes ne correspondent pas."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:233
msgid "Depending on the software the data may be irretrievably corrupted."
msgstr "Selon le logiciel, les données peuvent être irrémédiablement corrompues."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide19.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive19.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 19 - Review*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 19 - Récapitulatif*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:239
msgid "In review we have looked at the differences between the phrases:"
msgstr "En revue, nous avons examiné les différences entre les phrases :"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:241
msgid "Database; database language; database program, data-cleaning tool"
msgstr "Base de données ; langage de base de données ; logiciel de base de données ; outil de nettoyage des données"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:242
msgid "Field names & Field labels; Drop-down lists & Controlled vocabularies and between"
msgstr "Noms des champs & Libellés des champs ; Listes déroulantes & vocabulaires contrôlés et entre"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:243
msgid "Repertoires, Coded sets & Encodings"
msgstr "Répertoires de caractères, jeux de caractères codés et encodages"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:245
msgid "And shown that although the terms may seem similar the in fact have very different definitions."
msgstr "Et a montré que, malgré que les termes puissent sembler similaires, en fait, ont des définitions très différentes."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:246
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide20.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive20.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 20 - Wrap-up*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 20 - Conclusion*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:252
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:396
msgid "Remember that:"
msgstr "Souvienez-vous que:"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:254
msgid "“...The first step in wisdom is to know the things themselves; this notion consists in having a true idea of the objects.”"
msgstr "“...La première étape de la sagesse est de connaître les choses en elles-mêmes; cette notion consiste à avoir une idée réelle des objets.”"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:256
msgid "We often take for granted that there is a whole language associated with biodiversity informatics that is not commonplace and has to be learned. There is no shame in going back to basics and getting to grips with the vocabulary, grammar and syntax just like with any new language."
msgstr "Nous oublions souvent que l’informatique de la biodiversité possède son propre langage, composé de termes peu courants qu’il faut apprendre. Il est donc tout à fait normal de revenir aux notions de base afin de se familiariser avec son vocabulaire, sa grammaire et sa syntaxe, comme pour l’apprentissage de toute nouvelle langue."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:257
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-terminology-Slide21.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-terminologie-Diapositive21.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:260
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 21 - Conclusion*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 21 - Conclusion*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:262
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:406
msgid "This video is part of a series of presentations used in the GBIF Biodiversity Data Mobilization course. The biodiversity data mobilization curriculum was originally developed as part of the Biodiversity Information Development Programme funded by the European Union."
msgstr "Cette vidéo fait partie d'une série de présentations utilisées dans le cours de mobilisation des données de la biodiversité du GBIF.Le programme de mobilisation des données sur la biodiversité a été initialement développé dans le cadre du programme Biodiversity Information Development financé par l'Union européenne."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:264
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:716
msgid "This presentation was originally created and narrated by Sharon Grant with additional contributions by BID and BIFA Trainers, Mentors and Students."
msgstr "Cette présentation a été initialement créée et narrée par Sharon Grant avec des contributions supplémentaires des formateurs du BID et du BIFA, les Mentors et Étudiants."

#. type: Title ==
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:268
#, no-wrap
msgid "Software"
msgstr "====\tLogiciel"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:273
msgid "In this video (05:58), you will review examples of the different types of applications and software available in the world of biodiversity mobilization informatics."
msgstr "Dans cette vidéo (5 min 58 s), vous découvrirez différents exemples d’applications et de logiciels utilisés dans le domaine de l’informatique appliquée à la mobilisation des données sur la biodiversité."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:275
msgid "If you are unable to watch the embedded video, you can xref:attachment$foundations-software_v1-720p.mp4[download,opts=download] it locally. (MP4 - 23.5 MB)"
msgstr "Si vous ne parvenez pas à visionner la vidéo intégrée, vous pouvez la télécharger localement via le lien suivant :$foundations-software_v1-720p.mp4[download,opts=download]. (MP4 - 23,5 Mo)"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide1.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive1.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:295
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 1 - Foundations - Software terminology*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 1 - Fondations - Terminologie des logiciels*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:297
msgid "This session is foundation work and part of the Terminology section We will be introducing you to types of software used in data mobilization."
msgstr "Cette session fait partie du module « Fondation », dans la section consacrée à la terminologie. Elle présente les différents types de logiciels utilisés pour la mobilisation des données."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide2.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive2.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 2 - Software for mobilization*\n"
msgstr "Diapositive 2 – Logiciels pour la mobilisation des données\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:305
msgid "The purpose of this short presentation is to give you some examples of the different types of applications and software available in the world of biodiversity mobilization informatics."
msgstr "Cette courte présentation a pour objectif de vous faire découvrir quelques exemples d’applications et de logiciels utilisés dans le domaine de la mobilisation des données sur la biodiversité."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:307
msgid "Hopefully it will help you to start to think about what uses they may be put too and what types of things might be practical for you."
msgstr "Nous espérons qu’elle vous aidera à réfléchir aux différentes utilisations possibles de ces outils et à déterminer lesquels pourraient répondre concrètement à vos besoins."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:308
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide3.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive3.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:311
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 3 - Software definition*\n"
msgstr "Diapositive 3 – Définition d’un logiciel\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:313
msgid "So very briefly, a definition."
msgstr "Commençons par une brève définition."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:315
msgid "We are making a distinction here between all software and those applications which have been created for an end-user to carry out a task."
msgstr "Nous faisons ici la distinction entre les logiciels au sens large et les applications conçues pour permettre à un utilisateur final d’accomplir une tâche précise."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:317
msgid "We will take a look at software that can be used for:"
msgstr "Nous allons découvrir différents logiciels permettant de :"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:319
msgid "Data Capture"
msgstr "Capture des données ou saisie des données"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:320
msgid "Data Management"
msgstr "Gestion des données"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:321
msgid "Data Cleaning and"
msgstr "Nettoyage des données et"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:322
msgid "Data Publishing"
msgstr "Publication de données"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:323
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide4.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive4.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:326
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 4 - Software for data capture*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 4 – Logiciels de capture des données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:328
msgid "In the realm of data capture software, there is often no need to go “big” when capturing information initially, especially in the field."
msgstr "Pour la capture initiale des données, notamment sur le terrain, il n’est généralement pas nécessaire de recourir à des logiciels complexes ou très élaborés."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:330
msgid "You can capture information from collection specimens or live observations in a simple spreadsheet such as:"
msgstr "Vous pouvez enregistrer les informations issues de spécimens de collection ou d’observations sur le terrain dans un simple tableur, comme :"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:332
msgid "Excel, OpenOffice, LibreOffice or Google Sheets."
msgstr "Excel, OpenOffice, LibreOffice ou Google Sheets."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:334
msgid "There may even not be a need to create your own system at all. Apps such as iNaturalist, or eBird are stable, robust and have simple intuitive interfaces."
msgstr "Vous n’avez pas forcément besoin de concevoir votre propre système. Des applications telles qu’iNaturalist et eBird sont stables, fiables et faciles à utiliser grâce à leurs interfaces simples et intuitives."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:336
msgid "Whichever the choice, it is important to think about the long term preservation of the data that you collect."
msgstr "Quel que soit votre choix, assurez-vous que les données collectées resteront accessibles et utilisables à long terme."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:337
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide5.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive5.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:340
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 5 - Software for data management*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 5 - Logiciels de gestion des données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:342
msgid "So, depending on your needs, a more complex data management software might be the right solution for your data. Especially if long term retention and preservation is a priority."
msgstr "En fonction de vos besoins, il peut être préférable d’utiliser un logiciel de gestion des données plus complet, en particulier si vous souhaitez garantir leur conservation à long terme."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:344
msgid "More stable management platforms also better support sharing of data to multiple audiences."
msgstr "Des plateformes de gestion fiables permettent également de diffuser plus facilement les données auprès de différents types d’utilisateurs."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:346
msgid "There are many choices which vary in terms of cost and support and a few are shown here. From left to right:"
msgstr "Il existe de nombreuses options, qui diffèrent par leur coût et le niveau d’assistance proposé. En voici quelques-unes, présentées de gauche à droite :"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:348
msgid "Symbiota, Specify, EMu, Elysia and Brahms."
msgstr "Symbiota, Specify, EMu, Elysia et Brahms."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide6.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive6.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:352
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 6 - Software for data capture and management*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 6 – Logiciels de capture et de gestion des données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:354
msgid "If a home-grown solution is preferred and can be supported, relational database software can provide cheaper alternatives."
msgstr "Si vous optez pour une solution conçue en interne et que votre institution peut en assurer le soutien technique, les logiciels de bases de données relationnelles peuvent offrir une alternative plus économique."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:356
msgid "Examples incluse MySQL, SQLServer, Access or filemaker"
msgstr "Parmi les exemples, on peut citer MySQL, SQL Server, Access ou FileMaker"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:357
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide7.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive7.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:360
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 7 - Software for data cleaning*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 7 - Logiciels de nettoyage des données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:362
msgid "Increasingly the lines between languages, programs and tools have blurred, each being capable of many complex and overlapping functions. The common “Find and Replace” function is a good example of a data cleaning tool that is found in almost all database programs and is a command in database languages."
msgstr "La différence entre les langages, les logiciels et les outils est aujourd’hui moins évidente, car ils permettent souvent d’effectuer des tâches similaires.\n"
"La fonction « Rechercher et remplacer » en est un bon exemple : utilisée pour nettoyer les données, elle est disponible dans presque tous les logiciels de base de données et peut également être exécutée sous forme de commande dans les langages de base de données."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:364
msgid "You are probably already familiar with spreadsheets such as Excel and indeed these are probably the most common data cleaning tools available. However there are others."
msgstr "Vous connaissez probablement déjà les tableurs comme Excel, qui comptent parmi les outils de nettoyage des données les plus couramment utilisés. D’autres outils spécialisés sont également disponibles."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:366
msgid "OpenRefine originally known as GoogleRefine is a powerful free, open source data cleaning tool with a large support community. You will see more of this program in upcoming sessions."
msgstr "OpenRefine, auparavant connu sous le nom de Google Refine, est un logiciel libre, gratuit et performant destiné au nettoyage des données. Il bénéficie du soutien d’une importante communauté. Vous aurez l’occasion de l’utiliser davantage dans les prochaines sessions."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:368
msgid "R is another increasing used, sophisticated programming language and environment. With a little practice it can also provide powerful data manipulations."
msgstr "R est un langage et un environnement de programmation avancés dont l’utilisation ne cesse de se développer. Après une certaine prise en main, il offre de nombreuses possibilités pour traiter et transformer efficacement les données."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:369
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide8.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive8.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:372
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 8 - Software for data publishing*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 8 - Logiciels de publication de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:374
msgid "Planning further ahead to the sharing of your data through GBIF to the international scientific and deciders community you will need to choose a publishing tool."
msgstr "Lorsque vous serez prêt à diffuser vos données via le GBIF auprès de la communauté scientifique internationale et des décideurs, vous devrez choisir un outil de publication."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:376
msgid "The choice will depend largely on the level of infrastructure support at your institution. If this is high and stable, installing an IPT or BioCASe application may be the right option. But there are others if this is not the case."
msgstr "Le choix de l’outil dépendra en grande partie des infrastructures et de l’assistance technique dont dispose votre institution. Si elles sont fiables et durables, vous pouvez envisager d’installer un IPT ou BioCASe. Si ce n’est pas le cas, d’autres solutions de publication peuvent être utilisées."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:378
msgid "You can consider partnering with an existing ipt provider or selecting a database management system that includes a publishing pathway of its own."
msgstr "Vous pouvez également vous rapprocher d’une institution hébergeant déjà un IPT, ou opter pour un système de gestion de base de données doté de sa propre mécanisme de publication."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:380
msgid "Whichever you choose, make sure that your system allows you to export data as csv or txt files and you will ultimately be able to publish your data."
msgstr "Quel que soit votre choix, assurez-vous que le système permet d’exporter les données aux formats CSV ou TXT. Vous pourrez ainsi les publier par la suite."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:381
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide9.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive9.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:384
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 9 - Other software to handle data*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 9 - Autres logiciels de gestion des données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:386
msgid "This is a summary of the information collected in the course survey of software in use by students, mentors and trainers in the GBIF community."
msgstr "Ce résumé présente les informations recueillies lors d’une enquête sur les logiciels utilisés par les participants, les mentors et les formateurs de la communauté GBIF."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:388
msgid "The link and reference to more details of each section, is at the bottom of the slide."
msgstr "Le lien permettant d’accéder aux références et aux informations détaillées de chaque section figure au bas de la diapositive."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:390
msgid "Reference: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IWBsL4r-LsJRdYYPy9q4eLOAa1nzZYBwTdwk3Kd8cV8/"
msgstr "Référence : https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IWBsL4r-LsJRdYYPy9q4eLOAa1nzZYBwTdwk3Kd8cV8/"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:391
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide10.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive10.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:394
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 10 - Wrap-up*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 10 - Conclusion*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:398
msgid "“The purpose of software is to help people” and not the other way around."
msgstr "\"Le rôle d’un logiciel est d’aider les utilisateurs\", et non l’inverse."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:400
msgid "Your choice of solution should make your life easier but it should also not sacrifice the long term viability of the data that it is meant to work with."
msgstr "La solution choisie doit faciliter votre travail tout en permettant de préserver vos données et de les maintenir accessibles à long terme."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:401
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-software-Slide11.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-logiciels-Diapositive11.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:404
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 11 - Conclusion*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 11 - Conclusion*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:408
msgid "This presentation was narrated by Sharon Grant with additional contributions by BID and BIFA Trainers, Mentors and Students."
msgstr "Cette présentation a été narrée par Sharon Grant, avec les contributions complémentaires des formateurs, mentors et participants des programmes BID et BIFA."

#. type: Title ==
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:412
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structures"
msgstr "Structures"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:417
msgid "In this video (13:10), you will review the field and data types that hold data, the structures that help to organize and protect that data and what these mean for the integrity and security of your data."
msgstr "Dans cette vidéo (13 min 10 s), vous passerez en revue les différents types de champs et de données, les structures utilisées pour organiser et protéger ces données, ainsi que leur importance pour l’intégrité et la sécurité de vos données."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:419
msgid "If you are unable to watch the embedded video, you can xref:attachment$foundations-structures_v1-720p.mp4[download,opts=download] it locally.  (MP4 - 44.4 MB)"
msgstr "Si vous ne parvenez pas à visionner la vidéo intégrée, vous pouvez la télécharger localement via le lien suivant :$foundations-structures_v1-720p.mp4[download,opts=download].  (MP4 - 44,4 Mo)"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:436
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide1.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive1.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:439
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 1 - Foundations - Structures terminology*\n"
msgstr "Diapositive 1 – Fondation – Terminologie des structures\n"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:444
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide2.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive2.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:451
msgid "In the section on STRUCTURES we will be working on understanding the field and data types that hold data, the structures that help to organize and protect that data and lastly look at what these mean for the integrity and security of your data."
msgstr "Dans la section « STRUCTURES », nous examinerons les types de champs et de données, les structures qui permettent d’organiser et de protéger les données, puis leur importance pour l’intégrité et la sécurité de celles-ci."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:452
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide3.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive3.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:455
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 3 - Structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 3 - Structure*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:457
msgid "In this section on basic database Structures we will focus on the different elements that databases, software tools and languages use to handle the data that you enter."
msgstr "Dans cette section sur les structures de base, nous découvrirons les différents éléments utilisés par les bases de données, les logiciels et les langages pour traiter les données que vous saisissez."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:458
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide4.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive4.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:461
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 4 - Structures - Planes, trains and automobiles*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 4 – Structures : avions, trains et automobiles*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:463
msgid "First, lets look at field types, also known as data types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:464
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide5.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:467
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 5 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:469
msgid "Data Type lets the computer know what kind of data is expected in a particular field. This then dictates what functions can be performed on it."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:471
msgid "They can be simple and encompass a single concept or combine concepts depending on the software or language you are using. Either way the essential building blocks are the same."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:473
msgid "So let’s look at six that you will come across most frequently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:474
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide6.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:477
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 6 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:479
msgid "First Numeric fields – This data type holds numbers, and there are 2 kinds: "
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:481
msgid "Integers and long integers, hold whole numbers. For example 1, 2, 3, 99, 2000."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:483
msgid "The size of the number, depends on the number of bits assigned to the field (more about that later). For now just remember that a long integer field will hold a bigger number than an integer."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:485
msgid "Floats, also referred to as doubles, hold fractions or parts of whole numbers. For example 4.5, 19.47"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:487
msgid "The important thing to remember here is that a float always has decimal places so the number 10 will be stored as 10.0. The number of decimal places being an integral element of the type. This has implications when it comes to precision and accuracy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:488
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide7.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:491
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 7 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:493
msgid "Alphanumeric fields - are also referred to as text, character or string fields."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:495
msgid "They can hold any letter, number or symbol in the coded character set and usually have a defined character limit. Entering more characters than the character limit can often result in truncation and loss of data on save."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:496
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide8.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:499
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 8 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:501
msgid "Another type of text field that you will come across is the Unstructured text field, also known as memo, long char or blob fields."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:503
msgid "These types of field are used to hold large amounts of unformatted text and unlike alphanumeric fields may not have an obvious character limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:505
msgid "In simple systems, they are generally less flexible in terms of processing; for example sorting and indexing, than their smaller alphanumeric cousins."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:507
msgid "With decreased storage costs and the rise of NoSQL document-oriented database programs, such as MongoDB however, this is changing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:508
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide9.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:511
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 9 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:513
msgid "System Value fields have a double nature and what you see on the screen is not usually the actual value that the software is storing in memory. Date and time fields are the most common example of this type of field."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:515
msgid "In this example you typed “1 March 1971” into a cell in Excel and hit return."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:517
msgid "Now it says “1-Mar-71” in the cell AND “3/1/1971” in the functionbar."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:519
msgid "Excel is applying a display format to the cell, which you can change at will."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:521
msgid "HOWEVER, if you remove the format you see that what is actually being stored in the field is the number 25993.00!"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:523
msgid "So you can see that the field is actually a float. You should beware because that system value not be the same from software to software. Exports should to checked to make sure the actual date is exported and not the system value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:524
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide10.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:527
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 10 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:529
msgid "Boolean fields – also known as Binary fields only contain one of two values that represent a one or a zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:531
msgid "They are a special case of a System Value field as mentioned previously in that whilst the software actually saves a number it often displays values such as:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:536
msgid "Yes/No; Yes/no; Y/N; True/False. "
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:538
msgid "You should take care to find out which way around the system you are using translates."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:540
msgid "Is a 1 a yes or no?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:541
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide11.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:544
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 11 - Containers – field/data types*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:546
msgid "Structured Text fields are less common but mentioned here for completeness."
msgstr "Les champs de texte structuré, bien que moins fréquemment utilisés, sont inclus ici afin de présenter l’ensemble des types de champs."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:548
msgid "They are fields which can be either made up of combinations of the simple data types or even be defined by the data itself."
msgstr "Ces champs peuvent combiner plusieurs types de données simples ou être structurés en fonction des données qu’ils contiennent."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:550
msgid "Most often these are used in programming languages to allow flexibility and handling of complex concepts."
msgstr "Ils sont principalement utilisés dans les langages de programmation afin d’offrir davantage de flexibilité et de permettre la gestion de concepts complexes."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:552
msgid "An example is the factor field used in the R programming language, which is defined as a type vector containing a set of numeric codes with character-valued levels."
msgstr "Le type facteur (factor), utilisé dans le langage de programmation R, en est un exemple. Il s’agit d’un vecteur contenant des codes numériques associés à des niveaux représentés par des chaînes de caractères."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:554
msgid "Ref:  https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~nolan/stat133/Fall05/lectures/DataTypes4.pdf"
msgstr "Référence : https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~nolan/stat133/Fall05/lectures/DataTypes4.pdf"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:555
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide12.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive12.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:558
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 12 - Structures - planes, trains and automobiles*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 12 – Structures : avions, trains et automobiles*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:560
msgid "Now that you have an understanding of the field types used to represent your data elements let’s talk about the containers or structures, that many database programs and software use collate and display your data."
msgstr "Maintenant que vous connaissez les types de champs utilisés pour représenter les différents éléments de vos données, intéressons-nous aux conteneurs, ou structures, qu’utilisent de nombreux logiciels de base de données pour regrouper et afficher ces données."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:562
msgid "Reference: https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/data-structures/"
msgstr "Référence : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/data-structures/"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:563
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide13.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive13.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:566
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 13 - Containers - Data structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 13 - Conteneurs - Structures de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:568
msgid "First is the cell."
msgstr "Tout d'abord, la cellule."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:570
msgid "This is the smallest data structure, it holds a single value and has a single data type associated with it."
msgstr "Il s’agit de la plus petite structure de données : elle contient une seule valeur à laquelle est associé un seul type de données."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:571
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide14.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive14.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:574
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 14 - Data structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 14 - Structures de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:578
msgid "There is one concept that you should beware of when it comes to cells and that is the “empty cell”.    “An empty cell doesn’t necessarily mean an empty field.”"
msgstr "Concernant les cellules, il convient de prêter une attention particulière à la notion de « cellule vide ».\n"
"« Une cellule vide ne signifie pas nécessairement qu’un champ est vide. »"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:580
msgid "Some software “fills” an empty field with a System value based on the data type."
msgstr "Certains logiciels « remplissent » automatiquement un champ vide avec une valeur système définie en fonction du type de données."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:582
msgid "Examples are “NULL” “N A” or even zero!"
msgstr "Par exemple : « NULL », « N/A », ou même zéro !"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:583
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide15.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive15.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:586
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 15 - Containers - Data structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 15 - Conteneurs - Structures de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:588
msgid "As you start to organize cells you begin to build a grid. Grids have implied structure in the form of"
msgstr "En organisant plusieurs cellules, vous commencez à former une grille. Cette grille présente une structure implicite composée de"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:590
msgid "Rows"
msgstr "Lignes"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:591
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide16.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive16.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:594
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 16 - Containers - Data structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 16 - Conteneurs - Structures de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:596
msgid "And columns."
msgstr "Et les colonnes."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:597
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide17.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive17.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:600
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 17 - Containers - Data structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 17 - Conteneurs - Structures de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:602
msgid "When you organize cells into rows and columns, obviously, what you get is a grid!"
msgstr "Lorsque vous organisez des cellules en lignes et en colonnes, vous obtenez tout simplement une grille !"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:604
msgid "This is looks very much like a spreadsheet right?"
msgstr "On dirait vraiment un tableur, n'est-ce pas ?"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:606
msgid "Well, yes. The difference however between a spreadsheet grid and a table are the strength of the ties that hold the rows and columns together."
msgstr "Oui, tout à fait. La différence entre une grille de feuille de calcul et une table tient toutefois à la manière dont les lignes et les colonnes sont liées entre elles."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:607
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide18.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive18.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:610
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 18 - Structures - planes, trains and automobiles*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 18 – Structures : avions, trains et automobiles*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:612
msgid "So let’s now talk about those connections."
msgstr "Parlons donc maintenant de ces liens."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:614
msgid "What the implications for the integrity and security of your data of loose unenforced relationships between rows and columns?"
msgstr "Quelles peuvent être les conséquences de liens peu structurés et non contrôlés entre les lignes et les colonnes sur l’intégrité et la sécurité de vos données ?"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:615
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide19.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive19.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:618
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 19 - Data structures*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 19 - Structures de données*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:620
msgid "What actually makes a table useful are the connections that we create to give the data in the structure meaning."
msgstr "Une table devient réellement utile lorsque nous établissons des liens entre les données pour leur donner du sens."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:622
msgid "We intrinsically make patterns of attributes that turns data into information."
msgstr "Nous associons naturellement différents attributs pour créer des ensembles cohérents qui transforment les données en informations utiles."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:624
msgid "Rows become records and Columns become attributes"
msgstr "Les lignes deviennent des enregistrements et les colonnes, des attributs"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:626
msgid "In a spreadsheet however, the connections between cells are idiomatic, loose and un-enforced."
msgstr "Dans un tableur, en revanche, les relations entre les cellules sont implicites, flexibles et ne sont pas contrôlées par le système."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:628
msgid "It is easy for the attributes between the rows to get jumbled up or for the values get changed and then the meaning is lost."
msgstr "Les attributs peuvent facilement être mélangés entre les lignes ou les valeurs modifiées, entraînant ainsi une perte de sens."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:629
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide20.png"
msgstr "fondations::fondations-structures-Diapositive20.png"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:632
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 20 - Integrity and security*\n"
msgstr "*Diapositive 20 - Intégrité et sécurité*\n"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:634
msgid "This lack of enforced connections makes a spreadsheet easy to use but these same qualities also cause problems."
msgstr "L’absence de liens contrôlés rend les feuilles de calcul faciles à utiliser, mais elle peut aussi entraîner des problèmes."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:636
msgid "Errors are easy to make and hard to catch."
msgstr "Les erreurs sont faciles à commettre et difficiles à détecter."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:638
msgid "Connections and relationships are not documentable and so subject to interpretation and mutation."
msgstr "Les liens et les relations ne peuvent pas être clairement documentés ; ils sont donc sujets à interprétation et peuvent être modifiés."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:640
msgid "Spreadsheets are not built to scale either in terms of size or numbers of users."
msgstr "Les feuilles de calcul ne sont pas conçues pour gérer de grands volumes de données ni un nombre élevé d’utilisateurs."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:642
msgid "So can be slow, crashy and easily corruptible"
msgstr "Elles peuvent donc devenir lentes, instables et facilement être corrompues"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:644
msgid "Spreadsheets are easy to copy and email"
msgstr "Les feuilles de calcul sont faciles à copier et à envoyer par e-mail"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:646
msgid "So they are hard to version and keep track of"
msgstr "Le suivi des modifications et la gestion des versions deviennent donc difficiles"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:648
msgid "The question is what is the solution?"
msgstr "La question est : quelle est la solution ?"

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:650
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:688
msgid "Reference: https://www.mrc-productivity.com/blog/2014/09/7-dangers-of-spreadsheets-part-1/"
msgstr "Référence : https://www.mrc-productivity.com/blog/2014/09/7-dangers-of-spreadsheets-part-1/"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:651
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide21.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:654
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 21 - Containers - Integrity and security*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:656
msgid "Let’s look back, at the connections in a bit more detail."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:658
msgid "We generally understand that the data in each row of a table means something."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:660
msgid "For example each row can represent a specimen or a taxa that was found at a particular place, at a particular time, by a particular person."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:662
msgid "It would be odd to have one row in a table that represents a specimen followed by a row that represents a collection site."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:664
msgid "We also often want to analyse, sort and compare values of particular attributes between rows."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:666
msgid "For example you may want find the mean weight of all the Kenyan bats."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:668
msgid "So ideally we want to use a system to store our data that:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:670
msgid "always holds the rows together"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:671
msgid "does not mix data types"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:672
msgid "and segregates data in each table to a single concept or theme"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:674
msgid "These are functions of a database!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:675
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide22.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:680
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 22 - Integrity and security*\n"
" \n"
"Functions in a true database inherently bind rows together and columns may only have a single data type.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:682
msgid "Tables in database are held together by virtual links called keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:684
msgid "These keys are identifiers that match between tables and allow data to be connected efficiently."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:686
msgid "It is these 2 key concepts that distinguish a spreadsheet from a database."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:689
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide23.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:694
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 23 - Review*\n"
" \n"
"In review then, we have looked at the 6 most common data types, the basic building blocks of data structure and distinguished between a spreadsheet grid and database table.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:696
msgid "Understanding these elements and how they interact with one another will allow you to better determine the best ways to manipulate and document the data that falls under your custodianship."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:697
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide24.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:702
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Slide 24 - Wrap-up*\n"
" \n"
"Remember that: \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:704
msgid "“When you realize the difference between the container and the content, you will have knowledge.”"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:706
msgid "Using the correct terms to describe both your data and the structures that you create and use to store it; is the most important way to ensure that it remains relevant and useable."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:708
msgid "Never underestimate how much damage can be done to priceless information by careless descriptions and storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/foundations/modules/ROOT/pages/foundations-terminology.adoc:709
#, no-wrap
msgid "foundations::foundations-structures-Slide25.png"
msgstr ""

